Hi,

on the Desktop Architects Meeting 4 on the Linux Foundation Summit in 
Mountain View there will be scheduled a breakout session for printing, 
during the breakout time on Thursday, 2:45pm - 4:30pm.

On the preparation phone conference for the OpenPrinting Meeting on 
Friday we also talked about this breakout session and came to the 
following suggested agenda items:

- Desktop architects and LSB developers, especially if they will not
   join the OpenPrinting Meeting on Friday can discuss printing subjects
   with us, make suggestions, and leave us with more subjects and ideas
   to talk about on Friday.

- Discussion of desktop-related printing subjects, especially if desired
   by participants not being able to join the appropriate sessions on the
   OpenPrinting Meeting on Friday:

    o Distribution-independent printer driver packages and auto-download
      and installation of these packages by printer setup tools.

    o Printing dialog and GUI as worked on on the OpenPrinting
      Usability/GUI Meeting on the LinuxTag in Berlin.

    o Implementation of printing-related projects. See
      http://www.linux-foundation.org/en/OpenPrinting/Implementation

    o Other printing-related subjects which emerged from Desktop
      Architects Meeting

- Your suggestions welcome. Post them here on the list.

Everyone is invited to join. See you in mOuntain View.

    Till

